<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cleartext HTTP is permitted, deliberately, and this file is the reason the app
  shows pages instead of a blank screen.

  Since Android 9 cleartext is blocked by default. EduFlex is served by XAMPP
  over plain http on a laptop on the same network as the phone, or over a USB
  bridge, so without this every request fails with ERR_CLEARTEXT_NOT_PERMITTED
  and the WebView renders nothing. That failure gives no visible reason, which
  is how it costs an afternoon.

  A per-host list is not enough here: the laptop's LAN address changes with the
  network, and network-security-config matches domains, not subnets, so
  192.168.*.* cannot be expressed. A demo app that only ever talks to a machine
  in the same room is the one case where permitting cleartext broadly is the
  honest answer rather than a shortcut.

  WHEN EduFlex IS SERVED OVER HTTPS (Still to do, item 3), delete the
  base-config below and keep only the localhost entries. At that point
  security_is_https() turns on the Secure cookie flag and HSTS by itself, and
  leaving this file as it is would quietly undo part of that.
-->
<network-security-config>

    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />

    <!-- Named so the intent is recorded even though base-config already covers
         them. 10.0.2.2 is how the Android emulator reaches the host machine;
         localhost is what `adb reverse` maps to the laptop over USB. -->
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">localhost</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">127.0.0.1</domain>
        <domain includeSubdomains="false">10.0.2.2</domain>
    </domain-config>

</network-security-config>
